[usage]
[directions] d-19 [open] Deepen weakest claim 1: pure-Higgsino thermal relic mass and; d-20 [open] Deepen weakest claim 2: inelastic Higgsino explanation of LZ; d-21 [open] Close gaps on elastic SI loop cross section vs LZ 2024/XENON
[phase] critic-plan
[usage]
[critique] wave 0 plan: revise
[directions] d-19 [open] Deepen weakest claim 1: pure-Higgsino thermal relic mass and; d-20 [open] Deepen weakest claim 2: inelastic Higgsino explanation of LZ; d-21 [open] Close gaps on elastic SI loop cross section vs LZ 2024/XENON
**Plan** — 3 lines of investigation:
1. Deepen weakest claim 1: pure-Higgsino thermal relic mass and its uncertainty from Sommerfeld + bound-state formation. Contrast the simplistic serve-idm.sh perturbative result (~1.16 TeV) with literature values that include non-perturbative effects, and add one new paper beyond 1411.6930/2205.04486. — Prior d-01/d-04/d-09 left only one published Omega_h2 point (1411.6930 at 1172 GeV, 0.126/0.127) and a tool value at 1159 GeV that has no Sommerfeld, no coannihilation, no bound-state switch (f-021) and unreliable consistent_planck flag. The thermal target 1.0-1.1 TeV is quoted without spread. Need independent calculation with bound-state formation to quantify shift and uncertainty.
2. Deepen weakest claim 2: inelastic Higgsino explanation of LZ 248 keV event (delta~350 keV) vs solar-capture/IceCube exclusion (delta>566 keV). Contrast standard-halo tool prediction (zero events for delta>=400 keV) with halo-tail variation and add one new solar-capture paper. — Prior d-10 used serve-idm.sh predict_recoil with hard cutoff v_esc+v_E=776 km/s, no LMC high-speed tail option, and found 0 events for delta>=400 keV, contradicting 2609.01583 preferred region delta=481-519 keV, m_chi=1000-1183 GeV. Tool also treats annihilation as p-wave/splitting-suppressed (q-15), making Fermi/CMB passes unreliable. Solar capture rate C and IceCube limit ~1.5e19 s^-1 not computed. Tension hinges on halo tail, solar density/heavy elements, elastic cooling, and LZ sideband fit - all untested.
3. Close gaps on elastic SI loop cross section vs LZ 2024/XENONnT limits at 1 TeV and neutrino fog, with XLZD projection. — Prior d-02/d-05 left XENONnT 2303.14729 limit at 1 TeV unread, LZ 2410.17036 limit at 1 TeV unread (only 40 GeV point 2.2e-48 cm2 quoted), neutrino fog numeric missing, and f-008 arithmetic corrected but still based on linear extrapolation (~6e-47 cm2 at 1.1 TeV). Chen & Hill 1912.07795 upper bound <1e-48 cm2 quoted but not cited via cite(). Needed for purity constraints on gaugino mixing.
Critic's view: revise — Tool budget exceeded: 5x compute_relic_density + list_agent_files + list_files + 2-3x read_text_file + 2-3x web_search + 2-3x read_arxiv_chunk + 2x cite + describe_tools + get_paper_figures = ~17-19 calls >15 limit. Reduce to 3 mass points (e.g., 1000, 1159, 2800 GeV) and consolidate reads.; list_agent_files probes out/ and returned [] ; steps reference absolute path /Users/nramachandra/.../runs/261016_110437/ which requires list_files with explicit directory argument, not list_agent_files. Correct tool usage.; Tool budget massively exceeded: predict_recoil at 3 masses x 5 deltas =15 calls alone, plus predict_annual_modulation for same grid, plus 2x check_all_constraints, scan_mass_splitting, plot_recoil_spectrum, plot_constraint_summary, web_search, read_arxiv_chunk, cite, get_paper_figures >30 calls. Must prune to representative grid: e.g., 1 mass (1080 GeV) x 5 deltas for predict_recoil (5 calls) + 2x check_all_constraints + 1x scan_mass_splitting = within 15..
